From: ios-milanf-port (desk phase, 2026-10-21)
Subject: [PATCH] MILANF machine config: Moto G Stylus 5G (2022), SM6375

Sibling of 0004-sweet-machine-config.patch: same structure, same code
paths (the Group 1 IRQ routing in sleh.c / pe_fiq.c is shared, guarded
by defined(SWEET) || defined(MILANF)), with SM6375 substitutions:

- Kryo 660 = Cortex-A78 + Cortex-A55, ARMv8.2, no PAC: plain arm64,
  -march=armv8.2-a+crypto, 64-byte cache lines (cline 6), like SWEET.
- Architected timer PPIs are numbered 1/2/3/0 (secure phys, phys,
  virt, hyp) exactly as on SM7150, so CNTV is INTID 19 again.
  Source: mainline Linux arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375.dtsi, the
  `timer` node (compatible "arm,armv8-timer"); to be confirmed
  against the unit's own DTB, which stays the authority.
- GIC register offsets are architectural (Arm IHI 0069G) and are
  carried over unchanged. The GIC *addresses* differ from SM7150
  (0x0f200000, not 0x17a00000) but addresses live in the ADT
  (tools/mkadt-milanf.py), not in this header.

DESK-AUTHORED, NOT YET APPLIED OR BUILT: context lines are the
post-0004 tree state; first validation is the first MILANF CI/local
build (see BRINGUP.md). Applies after 0004 in the series order.

